WEBVTT

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.349
who gave me a full scholarship
to the United States.

00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:03.634
My mother still lived in a cow-dung hut,

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:05.681
none of my brothers were going to school,

00:01:05.706 --> 00:01:07.976
and this man told me, "Here, go."

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.035
I got a scholarship

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:11.698
to St. Lawrence University,
Upstate New York;

00:01:11.723 --> 00:01:12.762
finished that.

00:01:13.325 --> 00:01:16.925
And after that I went
to Harvard Graduate School;

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.188
finished that.

00:01:18.674 --> 00:01:20.396
Then I worked in DC a little bit:

00:01:20.421 --> 00:01:23.482
I wrote a book for National Geographic
and taught U.S. history.

00:01:23.507 --> 00:01:25.976
And every time, I kept going back home,

00:01:26.157 --> 00:01:27.625
listening to their problems --

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.195
sick people, people
with no water, all this stuff --